{"step_index":2185,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T14:48:15Z","input_tokens":2111,"cache_read_tokens":117807,"output_tokens":479,"content":"Yes, exactly. The **Btrfs send/receive on boot is the engine of automatic, atomic upgrades**:\n\n```\nHOST (Golden Release Slot)                            CONTAINER BOOT\n──────────────────────────                            ──────────────\nNew System Release Snapshot                            Container Awakens\n            │                                                 │\n            └─────────> [btrfs send | btrfs receive] ─────────┘\n                                   │\n                                   ▼\n                       Atomic Upgrade Layer Received\n                                   │\n                                   ▼\n             OverlayFS lowerdir=\"$upgrade_layer:$seed_layer\"\n             Container runs latest code instantly with 0 downtime\n```\n\n1. **How It Works**:\n   * When the container boots, `sync-instance-upgrade.sh` checks if a newer host release snapshot exists.\n   * If yes, it streams the differential delta via `btrfs send | btrfs receive` directly into the container's read-only upgrade layer.\n   * The container's root view assembles with OverlayFS using the new upgrade layer over the immutable seed.\n2. **Why It Is Atomic**:\n   * Btrfs send/receive transfers complete, read-only filesystem generations.\n   * A partial download or interrupted stream never activates.\n   * If an upgrade fails or is rejected, the container boots the previous generation instantly with zero broken dependencies.\n3. **Cozo Maintains the Pair**:\n   * The host-to-container pairing and generation IDs are recorded in Cozo, ensuring the container always aligns with its authoritative upgrade path across reboots.\n\n---\n\n### What I Will Do Next\n\nIn `/srv/git/3tched-container/scripts/launch-identity.sh`:\n* Call the canonical `sync-instance-upgrade.sh` helper during boot to execute the `btrfs send | btrfs receive` delta sync and mount the upgrade layer before the container processes awaken.\n\n---\n\n### Confirmation Request\n\nThis will integrate the existing, tested `sync-instance-upgrade.sh` boot hook into the identity launcher in `/srv/git/3tched-container`. It will not modify host storage pools or running containers.\n\n**Do you confirm wiring the boot-time send/receive upgrade hook into `launch-identity.sh`?**"}
